# A compound index keeps one actual boundary and its real pointer/index inputs.
fn: take (int: value) int
return: value
fn: work (@: int p; size_t: i) int
    p[i + 1U]: 29
return: take(p[i + 1U])
[]: int cells 2
cells[0]: 11
cells[1]: 12
int: result work(@cells[0], 0U)
if: result != 29 || cells[0] != 11 || cells[1] != 29
    result: 81
else:
    result: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
